  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The volume of water in a container can be modelled by the equation\n\n$$V=\\frac{10-t}{2+t},$$\n\nwhere $t$ is time in minutes and $V$ is measured in litres.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How much water was in the container initially?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\,\\mathrm{L}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V(0)&=\\frac{10-0}{2+0}\\\\V(0)&=5\\,\\mathrm{L}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $V'(t)=-\\frac{12}{(2+t)^2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$V'(t)=-\\frac{12}{(2+t)^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V'(t)&=\\frac{(-1)(2+t)-(10-t)(1)}{(2+t)^2}\\\\V'(t)&=\\frac{-2-t-10+t}{(2+t)^2}\\\\V'(t)&=-\\frac{12}{(2+t)^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p35-q5-c-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Explain why the container keeps losing water until it is empty.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p35-q5-c-hint",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hint:",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ],
                  "colour": "#268cff"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " Look at the sign of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "V'(t)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2+t)^2>0$ while the container holds water, so $V'(t)<0$ and the volume decreases.",
          "worked": "The numerator $10-t$ is positive for $0\\le t<10$ and is zero at $t=10$. Throughout that interval, $(2+t)^2>0$, so $V'(t)=-\\frac{12}{(2+t)^2}<0$. The volume therefore decreases until the container is empty.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the rate at which $V$ is decreasing initially.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\,\\mathrm{L/min}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V'(0)&=-\\frac{12}{(2+0)^2}\\\\V'(0)&=-3\\,\\mathrm{L/min}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe volume decreases at $3\\,\\mathrm{L/min}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find the rate at which $V$ is decreasing when $t=2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.75\\,\\mathrm{L/min}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V'(2)&=-\\frac{12}{(2+2)^2}\\\\V'(2)&=-0.75\\,\\mathrm{L/min}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe volume decreases at $0.75\\,\\mathrm{L/min}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      }
    ]
  },
